  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7688ac1a239c89eb58922876b61bff2f301f0ae8683ca3d64e73b00eb6fb953d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7688ac1a239c-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Catholic Social Services (CSS) holds the religious belief that marriage is a sacred bond between a man and a woman."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "City of Philadelphia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7688ac1a239c89eb58922876b61bff2f301f0ae8683ca3d64e73b00eb6fb953d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7688ac1a239c-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The City of Philadelphia argued that CSS\u2019s refusal to certify same\u2011sex couples violated a non\u2011discrimination provision in its contract and the citywide Fair Practices Ordinance."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7688ac1a239c89eb58922876b61bff2f301f0ae8683ca3d64e73b00eb6fb953d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7688ac1a239c-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Court, CSS alleged that the City\u2019s referral freeze violated the Free Exercise and Free Speech Clauses of the First Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. WINDHAM",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e49a8ecf586de441dadb8d91b0db06f5594d457b7cd9072e2a599c0cc1212099",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e49a8ecf586d-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Windham, the Court was asked whether the Free Exercise Clause \u201cshrinks every time the government expands its reach and begins to regulate work that has historically and traditionally been done by religious groups.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7688ac1a239c89eb58922876b61bff2f301f0ae8683ca3d64e73b00eb6fb953d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7688ac1a239c-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, Justice Alito framed the case as an \u201cimportant constitutional question\u201d about whether the Court\u2019s current interpretation of the Free Exercise Clause is fundamentally wrong."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e49a8ecf586de441dadb8d91b0db06f5594d457b7cd9072e2a599c0cc1212099",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e49a8ecf586d-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether the case involves a clash between free\u2011exercise rights and the rights recognized in Obergefell."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e49a8ecf586de441dadb8d91b0db06f5594d457b7cd9072e2a599c0cc1212099",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e49a8ecf586d-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas asked whether the dispute is about a contractual relationship or a regulatory/licensing scheme."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background & Legal Question",
    "status": "complete",
